    // ================= BOSSES =========================================

    {
      "id": "giantfrog2", "nameKey": "enemy.giantfrog2.name",
      // Bosses are horizontal strips, one region per animation. The brain
      // names the others: bosses/giantfrog2/{attack,charge,hit,jump}.
      "sprite": "bosses/giantfrog2/idle", "cell": 40,
      // 700 hit points. It was 900, which was right when the game was one
      // descent and a player arrived at floor 3 carrying four floors' worth of
      // relics; a stage starts from nothing, so the same 900 came to 117
      // seconds of unbroken swinging on the starting katana, and it went to
      // 520. Then characters got gear and a skill set each, and 520 went down
      // in seconds; 700 with a point of armour is back to a fight for a built
      // character and a long one, not an endless one, for a bare katana. See
      // BalanceTest.bossSeconds.
      //
      // Its blows were 12 and 22 until 2026-10-18, a tenth more than now: a
      // built character found its slam and its charge hit absurdly hard
      // ("đánh dame khá ảo") while the fight's length was fine, so only the
      // damage came down.
      "maxHp": 700, "contactDamage": 11, "attackDamage": 20, "moveSpeed": 51,
      "brain": "boss_frog", "aggroRange": 999, "attackRange": 72,
      "windupSteps": 30, "activeSteps": 18, "recoverSteps": 36, "cooldownSteps": 60,
      // Immovable. A boss that can be knocked back is a boss that can be
      // pinned against a wall and never allowed to act.
      "knockbackResist": 1.0, "hurtInvulnSteps": 6,
      "armour": 1, "attackSpeed": 1.15, "percentResist": 0.75,
      "lootTable": "boss_f3", "goldMin": 60, "goldMax": 100,
      "boss": true, "phases": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "tengured", "nameKey": "enemy.tengured.name",
      "sprite": "bosses/tengured/idle", "cell": 82,
      // The thief of the Kagebi, who fell through the island with it. 1120
      // across two phases of 560; at half hit points the fight stops and
      // plays bosses/tengured/trans, which is the only place the story is
      // told without a line of text.
      //
      // It was 1800, and stages made that unplayable rather than hard: nearly
      // four minutes of the same four attacks with the starting katana, since
      // nobody arrives at stage 5 with stage 1-4's relics any more. Still the
      // longest fight in the game at 880, which is what a last boss should be,
      // and 1120 once the cast had gear and skills to bring to it - with a
      // point of armour, a fifth more attack speed, and three quarters of any
      // percentage damage shrugged off, which is what the poisoner had been
      // killing it with.
      //
      // Its blows were 16 and 30 until 2026-10-18, a quarter more again in its
